WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.185 --> 00:00:22.339
After the frightening episode in the Gorbeau house, Marius moved into his friend Courfeyrac's apartment.

2
00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.622
Marius tried to work, but he was too distracted with worry.

3
00:00:27.183 --> 00:00:28.544
What had become of the Lark?

4
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.963
Every day he went to a park called The Field of the Lark and sat there thinking of

5
00:00:34.043 --> 00:00:38.726
her. One day in April, he heard a familiar voice call his name.

6
00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:43.990
Marius looked up and recognized the elder Thenardier girl, Eponine.

7
00:00:44.991 --> 00:00:50.675
She was still clothed in rags, but now she had straw in her hair, probably from sleeping in

8
00:00:50.715 --> 00:00:51.255
a stable.

9
00:00:52.015 --> 00:00:54.877
Despite this, she looked almost beautiful.

10
00:00:54.897 --> 00:01:01.494
"I spent two weeks in jail, and when I got out, you'd moved," said Eponine.

11
00:01:01.514 --> 00:01:04.695
"I've spent the last six weeks looking for you."

12
00:01:05.716 --> 00:01:06.856
Marius said nothing.

13
00:01:07.477 --> 00:01:10.739
He didn't want to have anything to do with this girl or her family.

14
00:01:10.759 --> 00:01:16.121
"I have the address you wanted me to get," said Eponine.

15
00:01:17.482 --> 00:01:18.643
Marius turned pale.

16
00:01:19.363 --> 00:01:20.044
"What address?"

17
00:01:20.064 --> 00:01:21.564
"For the young lady."

18
00:01:22.745 --> 00:01:25.206
Marius sprang from his seat and grabbed her hands.

19
00:01:25.226 --> 00:01:26.647
"Take me there at once!"

20
00:01:27.828 --> 00:01:29.729
"Oh, how happy you are!"

21
00:01:30.589 --> 00:01:33.732
A cloud crossed Eponine's face as she pulled away her hands.

22
00:01:33.752 --> 00:01:39.275
"Promise me, Eponine, that you won't tell your father—or anyone—where she is."

23
00:01:39.295 --> 00:01:44.339
"It's lovely to hear you say my name," Eponine said dreamily.

24
00:01:44.359 --> 00:01:45.660
"Promise me!"

25
00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.701
"All right, I promise.

26
00:01:48.401 --> 00:01:49.262
Now follow me."

27
00:01:50.323 --> 00:01:54.506
On the Rue Plumet, there stood a two-story house in a large garden.

28
00:01:55.426 --> 00:02:00.170
Behind this house was a smaller building and a gate leading onto another street.

29
00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:02.772
This is where Eponine led Marius.

30
00:02:04.093 --> 00:02:10.458
Several years earlier Jean Valjean had come to live there with Cosette and a female servant named Toussaint.

31
00:02:11.439 --> 00:02:15.963
While Cosette and Toussaint stayed in the main house, he slept in the smaller one.

32
00:02:17.464 --> 00:02:22.028
The neighbors didn't gossip about these new residents because there were no neighbors.

33
00:02:22.989 --> 00:02:28.068
Valjean rented the house using the name Ultimus Fauchelevent.

34
00:02:28.108 --> 00:02:31.930
Before then, Valjean and Cosette had been living happily at the convent.

35
00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:35.792
But as time passed Valjean began to feel guilty.

36
00:02:36.912 --> 00:02:40.234
If they stayed, he knew that Cosette would become a nun.

37
00:02:40.914 --> 00:02:45.516
It wouldn't be fair to make her retreat from life without first experiencing it.

38
00:02:46.456 --> 00:02:50.278
He also didn't want her to blame him if she ever regretted becoming a nun.

39
00:02:51.278 --> 00:02:57.173
Five years had passed since their arrival at the convent, and few people in the outside world would

40
00:02:57.253 --> 00:02:58.233
recognize him now.

41
00:02:59.274 --> 00:03:05.837
Besides, Cosette had almost completed her education, so Valjean decided it was time to move out.

42
00:03:06.977 --> 00:03:12.239
He paid the nuns for Cosette's education, and then the two of them left the convent.

43
00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:17.401
In addition to the Rue Plumet house, he had rented two other apartments.

44
00:03:18.402 --> 00:03:24.672
One was on the Rue de l'Ouest and the other on the Rue de l'Homme Armé.

45
00:03:24.712 --> 00:03:28.055
Never again would he be trapped as he'd been at the Gorbeau house.

46
00:03:28.895 --> 00:03:32.118
Every month or so, they moved from one house to another.

47
00:03:33.098 --> 00:03:39.423
Wherever they moved, he took the small suitcase containing the mourning outfit he had brought to the Thenardiers'

48
00:03:39.523 --> 00:03:45.347
inn. Cosette didn't know what was inside the suitcase, but she liked to tease him about it.

49
00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:48.169
"You're inseparable from that thing.

50
00:03:48.529 --> 00:03:49.530
I'm quite jealous!"

51
00:03:50.651 --> 00:03:54.514
As the years passed, Cosette began to grow more beautiful.

52
00:03:55.114 --> 00:03:59.017
She abandoned her convent school uniform for more fashionable clothing.

53
00:04:00.017 --> 00:04:03.039
Her growing beauty caused Valjean a deep anguish.

54
00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:04.841
Men would notice her.

55
00:04:05.441 --> 00:04:08.043
It was likely that someday she would leave him.

56
00:04:09.003 --> 00:04:12.025
It was about this time that Marius noticed Cosette's beauty.

57
00:04:12.806 --> 00:04:15.968
She also noticed Marius and fell in love with him.

58
00:04:17.109 --> 00:04:21.472
Observing this, Valjean stopped taking her to the Luxembourg Gardens.

59
00:04:22.944 --> 00:04:28.186
Cosette did not protest because she didn't want Valjean to know that she was interested in Marius.

60
00:04:28.926 --> 00:04:33.068
Instead she simply looked sad, which made Valjean sad.

61
00:04:34.029 --> 00:04:39.711
Cosette continued to sit with her father every evening and to accompany him when he brought food and

62
00:04:39.751 --> 00:04:40.831
clothing to the poor.

63
00:04:41.872 --> 00:04:47.474
The day after their visit to the Thenardiers, Valjean arrived home with a large burn on his arm.

64
00:04:48.114 --> 00:04:49.875
It took more than a month to heal.

65
00:04:50.895 --> 00:04:54.369
At the beginning of April, Valjean went away for a few days.

66
00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:58.052
He often did this when they needed money to run the household.

67
00:04:59.273 --> 00:05:04.416
One evening Cosette was sitting alone in the parlor when she heard footsteps in the garden.

68
00:05:05.497 --> 00:05:09.340
She ran up to her room and looked outside, but no one was there.

69
00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:13.502
Cosette thought no more about it; she was not easily startled.

70
00:05:14.483 --> 00:05:18.686
The next evening she was walking in the garden when she thought she saw a shadow.

71
00:05:19.607 --> 00:05:21.108
It looked like a man wearing a hat.

72
00:05:22.124 --> 00:05:25.365
For a moment she could not speak or turn her head.

73
00:05:26.785 --> 00:05:29.066
But then she gathered her courage and turned around.

74
00:05:29.946 --> 00:05:30.766
No one was there.

75
00:05:31.947 --> 00:05:35.368
Cosette looked behind bushes and in the dark corners of the garden.

76
00:05:35.888 --> 00:05:37.508
Still she found no one.

77
00:05:38.829 --> 00:05:42.890
When Valjean returned the next day, Cosette told him what had happened.

78
00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:47.571
She expected him to say, "Oh, you were just being a foolish girl."

79
00:05:48.611 --> 00:05:52.666
Instead he looked anxious and announced that he would search the garden.

80
00:05:53.306 --> 00:05:55.027
That night he summoned her outside.

81
00:05:55.047 --> 00:05:58.009
"Look, I've found your man with the hat."

82
00:05:58.409 --> 00:06:01.612
Valjean pointed to a chimney making a shadow on the grass.

83
00:06:02.552 --> 00:06:03.513
Cosette smiled.

84
00:06:03.533 --> 00:06:06.535
"I was just being foolish," she said.

85
00:06:07.115 --> 00:06:10.518
But this shadow didn't disappear when she turned around to look at it.

86
00:06:11.358 --> 00:06:16.081
A few nights later, Valjean was out, and Cosette was sitting on a bench in the garden.

87
00:06:17.202 --> 00:06:19.364
She decided to stroll among the plants.

88
00:06:20.064 --> 00:06:23.247
When she returned to her bench, there was a stone on it.

89
00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:27.090
"That wasn't there before," she said to herself.

90
00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:28.531
"Who put it there?"

91
00:06:29.752 --> 00:06:34.056
She ran into the house and told Toussaint to lock all the doors and windows.

92
00:06:35.076 --> 00:06:37.438
The next morning Cosette felt rather silly.

93
00:06:37.458 --> 00:06:41.402
"There was no stone on that bench, just as there was no man with a hat!"

94
00:06:42.663 --> 00:06:45.825
She went boldly into the garden and marched right up to the bench.

95
00:06:46.406 --> 00:06:48.948
The stone was holding down a letter on the bench.

96
00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:54.164
The envelope did not have a name on it, but Cosette assumed it was meant for her.

97
00:06:55.384 --> 00:06:59.428
She opened it and found four pieces of paper covered with writing.

98
00:07:00.408 --> 00:07:02.130
There was no signature at the end.

99
00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:07.514
Cosette began to read and immediately realized this was a love letter.

100
00:07:08.515 --> 00:07:09.576
Who could have written it?

101
00:07:10.216 --> 00:07:11.317
Cosette had no doubts.

102
00:07:12.098 --> 00:07:15.100
It was from the handsome young man in the Luxembourg Gardens.

103
00:07:16.281 --> 00:07:19.704
She carried the letter up to her room and spent the day rereading it.

104
00:07:21.172 --> 00:07:23.174
That night she went out into the garden.

105
00:07:24.034 --> 00:07:26.716
Marius stepped onto the path in front of her.

106
00:07:26.736 --> 00:07:28.798
"Forgive me if I've frightened you.

107
00:07:29.838 --> 00:07:34.281
My heart is bursting with love, and I couldn't remain hidden one moment longer."

108
00:07:35.302 --> 00:07:40.065
Marius explained how he had lurked in the garden and watched her the past few nights.

109
00:07:40.806 --> 00:07:42.067
Cosette took his hand.

110
00:07:42.087 --> 00:07:44.949
"Does this mean that you love me too?"

111
00:07:45.389 --> 00:07:46.170
asked Marius.

112
00:07:47.351 --> 00:07:49.032
She nodded and then they kissed.

113
00:07:49.676 --> 00:07:54.199
They talked for hours, describing how they had adored each other from afar.

114
00:07:55.100 --> 00:08:01.244
When they had told each other almost everything, Cosette laid her head on his shoulder and said, "My

115
00:08:01.304 --> 00:08:02.445
name is Cosette.

116
00:08:03.166 --> 00:08:03.826
What's yours?"

117
00:08:04.707 --> 00:08:09.150
"Marius." Cosette never asked Marius how he got into the garden.

118
00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:12.192
It seemed so natural that he was there.
